{"authored" [{"question" "q-46831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+2}-2}{{x}^{2}-4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/state.json" "file_sha256" "422c2f4302b0cbe36e99610fabed92eba8c8551f4a10947bf1bde4396725cc24" "basis" 586 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-46831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+2}-2}{{x}^{2}-4} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2+2}-2}{{2}^{2}-4}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+2}-2}{{x}^{2}-4} & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+2}-2}{(x-2)(x+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x+2}-2)(\\sqrt{x+2}+2)}{(x-2)(x+2)(\\sqrt{x+2}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{{(\\sqrt{x+2})}^{2}-{2}^{2}}{(x-2)(x+2)(\\sqrt{x+2}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x+2-4}{(x-2)(x+2)(\\sqrt{x+2}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x-2}{(x-2)(x+2)(\\sqrt{x+2}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{1}{(x+2)(\\sqrt{x+2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(2+2)(\\sqrt{2+2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/state.json" "file_sha256" "422c2f4302b0cbe36e99610fabed92eba8c8551f4a10947bf1bde4396725cc24" "basis" 586 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-46831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "