f4302b0cbe36e99610fabed92eba8c8551f4a10947bf1bde4396725cc24" "basis" 586 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-46831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\infty "] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/state.json" "file_sha256" "422c2f4302b0cbe36e99610fabed92eba8c8551f4a10947bf1bde4396725cc24" "basis" 586 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-46831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{DNE}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/state.json" "file_sha256" "422c2f4302b0cbe36e99610fabed92eba8c8551f4a10947bf1bde4396725cc24" "basis" 586 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{z-6}{\\sqrt{3z-2}-4}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/state.json" "file_sha256" "422c2f4302b0cbe36e99610fabed92eba8c8551f4a10947bf1bde4396725cc24" "basis" 586 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $z=6,$ we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{z-6}{\\sqrt{3z-2}-4} & =\\frac{6-6}{\\sqrt{3(6)-2}-4}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{z-6}{\\sqrt{3z-2}-4} & ={lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{(z-6)(\\sqrt{3z-2}+4)}{(\\sqrt{3z-2}-4)(\\sqrt{3z-2}+4)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{(z-6)(\\sqrt{3z-2}+4)}{(\\sqrt{3z-2})^{2}-{4}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{(z-6)(\\sqrt{3z-2}+4)}{(3z-2)-16} \\\\  & ={lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{(z-6)(\\sqrt{3z-2}+4)}{3z-18} \\\\  & ={lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{(z-6)(\\sqrt{3z-2}+4)}{3(z-6)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{\\sqrt{3z-2}+4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3(6)-2}+4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/state.json" "file_sha256" "422c2f4302b0cbe36e99610fabed92eba8c8551f4a10947bf1bde4396725cc24" "basis" 586 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6448eed90c99b1e57eadbdae2ab806c9e6324ee539b1c5234c728a5312453cd6" "basis" 586 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338515" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/state.json" "file_sha256" "422c2f4302b0cbe36e99610fabed92eba8c8551f4a10947bf1bde4396725cc24" "basis" 586 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-4463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{0+4}-2}{0}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x+4}-2)(\\sqrt{x+4}+2)}{x(\\sqrt{x+4}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x+4-4}{x(\\sqrt{x+4}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+4}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{0+4}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0c9e17a10adfc0320287732d151ca51250173d99882edfdc43daf2517459383"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\infty "] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-338481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{8-\\sqrt{8x}}{x-8}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-338481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to }\\frac{8-\\sqrt{8x}}{x-8} & =\\frac{8-\\sqrt{8(8)}}{8-8}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{8-\\sqrt{8x}}{x-8} & ={lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{(8-\\sqrt{8x})(8+\\sqrt{8x})}{(x-8)(8+\\sqrt{8x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{{8}^{2}-(\\sqrt{8x})^{2}}{(x-8)(8+\\sqrt{8x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{64-8x}{(x-8)(8+\\sqrt{8x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{-8(x-8)}{(x-8)(8+\\sqrt{8x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{-8\\cancel{(x-8)}}{\\cancel{(x-8)}(8+\\sqrt{8x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{-8}{8+\\sqrt{8x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{8+\\sqrt{8(8)}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{8+8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-338481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0c9e17a10adfc0320287732d151ca51250173d99882edfdc43daf2517459383"} {"question" "q-338481" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-338481" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-9}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-9} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3+1}-2}{{3}^{2}-9}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-9} & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{(x-3)(x+3)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x+1}-2)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)}{(x-3)(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{(\\sqrt{x+1})}^{2}-{2}^{2}}{(x-3)(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x+1-4}{(x-3)(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{(x-3)(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{1}{(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(3+3)(\\sqrt{3+1}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0c9e17a10adfc0320287732d151ca51250173d99882edfdc43daf2517459383"} {"question" "q-4468" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4468" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{24}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\infty "] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4468" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{24}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-338484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-x-6}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-338484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-x-6} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3+1}-2}{{3}^{2}-3-6}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-x-6} & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x+1}-2)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)}{({x}^{2}-x-6)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x+1})^{2}-{2}^{2}}{(x+2)(x-3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x+1)-4}{(x+2)(x-3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{(x+2)(x-3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{1}{(x+2)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(3+2)(\\sqrt{3+1}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-338484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0c9e17a10adfc0320287732d151ca51250173d99882edfdc43daf2517459383"} {"question" "q-338484" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-338484" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{20}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-46831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+2}-2}{{x}^{2}-4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-46831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+2}-2}{{x}^{2}-4} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2+2}-2}{{2}^{2}-4}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+2}-2}{{x}^{2}-4} & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+2}-2}{(x-2)(x+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x+2}-2)(\\sqrt{x+2}+2)}{(x-2)(x+2)(\\sqrt{x+2}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{{(\\sqrt{x+2})}^{2}-{2}^{2}}{(x-2)(x+2)(\\sqrt{x+2}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x+2-4}{(x-2)(x+2)(\\sqrt{x+2}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x-2}{(x-2)(x+2)(\\sqrt{x+2}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{1}{(x+2)(\\sqrt{x+2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(2+2)(\\sqrt{2+2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-46831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0c9e17a10adfc0320287732d151ca51250173d99882edfdc43daf2517459383"} {"question" "q-46831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-46831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{24}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "\\infty "] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-46831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{16}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+5}-\\sqrt{5}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=0$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+5}-\\sqrt{5}} & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{0+5}-\\sqrt{5}}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+5}-\\sqrt{5}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5})}{(\\sqrt{x+5}-\\sqrt{5})(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5})}{{(\\sqrt{x+5})}^{2}-{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5})}{x+5-5} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5})}{x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+5}+\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0c9e17a10adfc0320287732d151ca51250173d99882edfdc43daf2517459383"} {"question" "q-4467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-338515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{z-6}{\\sqrt{3z-2}-4}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-338515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $z=6,$ we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{z-6}{\\sqrt{3z-2}-4} & =\\frac{6-6}{\\sqrt{3(6)-2}-4}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{z-6}{\\sqrt{3z-2}-4} & ={lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{(z-6)(\\sqrt{3z-2}+4)}{(\\sqrt{3z-2}-4)(\\sqrt{3z-2}+4)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{(z-6)(\\sqrt{3z-2}+4)}{(\\sqrt{3z-2})^{2}-{4}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{(z-6)(\\sqrt{3z-2}+4)}{(3z-2)-16} \\\\  & ={lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{(z-6)(\\sqrt{3z-2}+4)}{3z-18} \\\\  & ={lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{(z-6)(\\sqrt{3z-2}+4)}{3(z-6)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{z\\to 6}\\frac{\\sqrt{3z-2}+4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3(6)-2}+4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-338515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0c9e17a10adfc0320287732d151ca51250173d99882edfdc43daf2517459383"} {"question" "q-338515" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-338515" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{x-1}{x-\\sqrt{x}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=1$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{x-1}{x-\\sqrt{x}} & =\\frac{1-1}{1-\\sqrt{1}}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{x-1}{x-\\sqrt{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{(x-1)(x+\\sqrt{x})}{(x-\\sqrt{x})(x+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{(x-1)(x+\\sqrt{x})}{{x}^{2}-{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{(x-1)(x+\\sqrt{x})}{{x}^{2}-x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{(x-1)(x+\\sqrt{x})}{x(x-1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{x+\\sqrt{x}}{x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{1+\\sqrt{1}}{1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0c9e17a10adfc0320287732d151ca51250173d99882edfdc43daf2517459383"} {"question" "q-4471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{x+3}-2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=1$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{x+3}-2} & =\\frac{1-1}{\\sqrt{1+3}-2}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{x+3}-2} & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{(x-1)(\\sqrt{x+3}+2)}{(\\sqrt{x+3}-2)(\\sqrt{x+3}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{(x-1)(\\sqrt{x+3}+2)}{{(\\sqrt{x+3})}^{2}-{2}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{(x-1)(\\sqrt{x+3}+2)}{x+3-4} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{(x-1)(\\sqrt{x+3}+2)}{x-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}(\\sqrt{x+3}+2) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+3}+2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0c9e17a10adfc0320287732d151ca51250173d99882edfdc43daf2517459383"} {"question" "q-4464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-4464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-338496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{4x-1}{2x-\\sqrt{x}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-338496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=\\frac{1}{4}$ we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{4x-1}{2x-\\sqrt{x}} & =\\frac{(4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}-1)}{(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}-\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}})}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{4x-1}{2x-\\sqrt{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{(4x-1)(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{(2x-\\sqrt{x})(2x+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{(4x-1)(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{(2x)^{2}-(\\sqrt{x})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{(4x-1)(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{4{x}^{2}-x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{(4x-1)(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{x(4x-1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{\\cancel{(4x-1)}(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{x\\cancel{(4x-1)}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{2x+\\sqrt{x}}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}})}{(\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-338496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0c9e17a10adfc0320287732d151ca51250173d99882edfdc43daf2517459383"} {"question" "q-338496" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "q-338496" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "6239c54542e17b36f7b4daf6add963bc39b69af2785ce63ee676d700b12d4c1f"} {"question" "e-74" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x - 2\\sqrt{x}} {x - 4} }.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/example-74.json" "file_sha256" "849f4caa91600db7bb93204342c6a29d7cbf3630cc9db68c8cbd89cbebbbcd56"} {"question" "e-74" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}\\frac{x-2\\sqrt{x}}{x-4} & =\\frac{4-2\\sqrt{4}}{4-4}=\\frac{0}{0},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x - 2\\sqrt{x}} {x - 4} &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {(x -2 \\sqrt{x})(x+2\\sqrt x)} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\n            &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x^2-\\left(2\\sqrt{x}\\right)^2} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\n\t    &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x^2-4x} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\n\t    &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x(x-4)} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\n\t    &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x} {x+2\\sqrt x} \\\n\t    &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {4} {4+2\\sqrt4} \\\n\t    &=\\dfrac 1 2.\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/example-74.json" "file_sha256" "849f4caa91600db7bb93204342c6a29d7cbf3630cc9db68c8cbd89cbebbbcd56"} {"question" "e-75" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac {3x} {\\sqrt{x +1} -1}  }.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/example-75.json" "file_sha256" "acc1c153f25e65660d73d9f6ba564ceb22ed7b21926a59b8a57328136ad583dc"} {"question" "e-75" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=0$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{x+1}-1} & =\\frac{3\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{0+1}-1}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac {3x} {\\sqrt{x + 1} - 1} \n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(3x)(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{(\\sqrt{x + 1} - 1)(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{\\left(\\sqrt{x+1}\\right)^2-1^2}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{x+1-1}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{x}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}3(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)\\\n&=3(\\sqrt{0+1}+1)\\\n\t&=6.\n}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/example-75.json" "file_sha256" "acc1c153f25e65660d73d9f6ba564ceb22ed7b21926a59b8a57328136ad583dc"}] "usage" {"e-75" [] "q-46831" [] "q-4464" [] "q-338515" [] "q-4463" [] "e-74" []} "basis" 1271 "retractions" [[17592186078841 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\lim_{x \\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x + 4} - 2}{x}$."] [17592186078842 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\lim_{x \\to 1^{-}}\\frac{x - 1}{\\sqrt{x + 3} - 2}$."] [17592186078279 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x - 2\\sqrt{x}} {x - 4}}$."] [17592186078279 :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lim_{x \\to 4^{+}}\\frac{x - 2\\sqrt{x}}{x - 4} &= \\frac{4 - 2\\sqrt{4}}{4 - 4} = \\frac{0}{0}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x - 2\\sqrt{x}} {x - 4} &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {(x -2 \\sqrt{x})(x+2\\sqrt x)} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\\ &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x^2-\\left(2\\sqrt{x}\\right)^2} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\\ &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x^2-4x} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\\ &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x(x-4)} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\\ &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x} {x+2\\sqrt x} \\\\ &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {4} {4+2\\sqrt4} \\\\ &=\\dfrac 1 2. \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186078280 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac {3x} {\\sqrt{x +1} -1}}$."] [17592186078280 :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=0$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lim_{x \\to 0}\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{x + 1} - 1} &= \\frac{3 \\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{0 + 1} - 1} = \\frac{0}{0}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac {3x} {\\sqrt{x + 1} - 1} &=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(3x)(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{(\\sqrt{x + 1} - 1)(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)} \\\\ &=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{\\left(\\sqrt{x+1}\\right)^2-1^2} \\\\ &=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{x+1-1} \\\\ &=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{x} \\\\ &=\\lim_{x\\to 0}3(\\sqrt{x+1}+1) \\\\ &=3(\\sqrt{0+1}+1) \\\\ &=6. \\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186076258 17592186076259 17592186076260 17592186076261 17592186076262 17592186076264 17592186076265 17592186076266 17592186076267 17592186076268 17592186264522 17592186264523 17592186264533 17592186264534 17592186264535 17592186264536 17592186264537] "immutable_fields" [[17592186076257 :answer-field/correct] [17592186076257 :answer-field/id] [17592186076257 :answer-field/key] [17592186076257 :answer-field/type] [17592186076263 :answer-field/correct] [17592186076263 :answer-field/id] [17592186076263 :answer-field/key] [17592186076263 :answer-field/type] [17592186264521 :answer-field/correct] [17592186264521 :answer-field/id] [17592186264521 :answer-field/key] [17592186264521 :answer-field/type] [17592186264532 :answer-field/correct] [17592186264532 :answer-field/id] [17592186264532 :answer-field/key] [17592186264532 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
